---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import DummyDataGenerator from '../../components/DummyDataGenerator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="SQL Dummy Data Generator" description="Define a simple schema and generate INSERT statements with realistic fake data for testing.">
  <DummyDataGenerator client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>Why fake data instead of real data</h2>
  <p>Seeding a dev or staging database with realistic-looking data lets you test queries, pagination, and UI without exposing real user records.</p>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Using unrealistic dummy data</strong> (like all identical values) that doesn't exercise edge cases your real data would actually contain.</li>
    <li><strong>Accidentally using production data instead</strong> for testing, exposing real user information in a less secure environment.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Seeding a development database with realistic test data</li>
    <li>Populating a demo environment without using real user records</li>
    <li>Testing pagination and query performance with a realistic data volume</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
